278	/* [BEVEL NOTE] Note on the beveling process:
279	
280		Each of the bevel_vertex, bevel_edge, and extrude_face functions do not represent
281		a full bevel/extrude operation. Instead, they should update the _connectivity_ of
282		the mesh, _not_ the positions of newly created vertices. In fact, you should set
283		the positions of new vertices to be exactly the same as wherever they "started from."
284	
285		When you click on a mesh element while in bevel mode, one of those three functions
286		is called. But, because you may then adjust the distance/offset of the newly
287		beveled face, we need another method of updating the positions of the new vertices.
288	
289		This is where bevel_positions and extrude_positions come in: these functions are
290		called repeatedly as you move your mouse, the position of which determines the
291		amount / shrink parameters. These functions are also passed an array of the original
292		vertex positions, stored just after the bevel/extrude call, in order starting at
293		face->halfedge->vertex, and the original element normal, computed just *before* the
294		bevel/extrude call.
295	
296		Finally, note that the amount, extrude, and/or shrink parameters are not relative
297		values -- you should compute a particular new position from them, not a delta to
298		apply.
299	*/
300	
